# Auth and permissions

- Sign-in is the Instanvi hub SSO handoff (same as Payroll, Pay, Talk): `src/proxy.ts` sends anonymous users to `${NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPER_APP_URL}/login`, the hub returns to `/auth-callback?payload=...`, which runs next-auth `signIn('session-sync')` and `hydrateAuthContext()`.
- `src/store/use-auth-context-store.ts` is the single source of truth for organization, location, hierarchy, roles and permissions (filled from IdP `/get-session`, `/session/permissions`, `/session/hierarchy`). Do not add another permission store or read permissions from the next-auth session.
- Location: the user picks it in the header `LocationSwitcher`; `x-location-id` follows the store. After changing it, invalidate queries (the switcher already does).
- Gate UI with `<Can resource="Invoice" action="create">...</Can>` or `useCan().canAccess(resource, action)`. Org admins/owners pass automatically.
- Resource/action strings must match potta-backend's `@Permissions({ action, resource })` exactly (e.g. `SalesReciept`, `JournalEntries`, `BankAccounts`). The catalog is `src/lib/permissions.ts`; keep it in sync with instanvi-auth-starter `src/roles/potta-permissions.catalog.ts`.
- New routes need an entry in `src/lib/route-permissions.ts` (longest prefix wins) so the sidebar hides them for users without access.
- Public pages (no session): `/login`, `/auth-callback`, `/vendor-portal/**`, `/unauthorized`. Keep `src/proxy.ts` and `src/auth.config.ts` in sync when adding one.
- Sign out with `signOutWithAuthApi()` from `src/lib/auth-sign-out.ts`, behind a confirmation dialog.
